# Numerical convergence of the molecule (paper table tab-conv-mol): triplet H2, bond parallel to B, at the
# optimized R_e = 0.236753 bohr of 11opt (ropt_R0.24.log, geo 3), single points (no ropt). Base = the production
# settings of 11/11opt (rcut 0.75); each other line changes ONE setting, the same for H2 and the H atom, so both E(H2)
# and D = 2E(H) - E(H2) can be followed. tolscf/tol tightened to 1e-7 so the SCF error stays below the effects.
# Written by hand 2026-10-22 (user request).
COMMON B=425.5 k=10 thresh=1e-6 eprec=1e-9 L=8 qextra=10 h=0.25 tmin=1e-8 tmax_factor=45 dphi=3 inner=3 rcut=0.75 rtaper=0.075
H2_base       nelec=2 state=triplet axial=1 ma=0 mb=-1 E0=203.5 E0b=207.7 tolscf=1e-7 maxscf=40 "atoms=1,0,0,-0.118376;1,0,0,0.118376"
H2_k8         nelec=2 state=triplet axial=1 ma=0 mb=-1 E0=203.5 E0b=207.7 tolscf=1e-7 maxscf=40 "atoms=1,0,0,-0.118376;1,0,0,0.118376" k=8
H2_k12        nelec=2 state=triplet axial=1 ma=0 mb=-1 E0=203.5 E0b=207.7 tolscf=1e-7 maxscf=40 "atoms=1,0,0,-0.118376;1,0,0,0.118376" k=12
